     "text": "{\"reachable\": true, \"rationale\": \"With h1_0:reach and h5_1:reach blocked, the target is still reachable through h5_2:obtain. From the entry footholds edge0:reach and edge1:reach: h1_1:access (OR) and h1_2:access (AND, both entries) are reached. Then h2_0:traverse (h1_1 + edge0), h2_1:access (h1_1 + h1_2) and h2_2:reach (edge1) are reached. h3_0:traverse (h2_0 + h2_2) and h3_2:traverse (via h2_0) follow. h4_0:obtain (via h2_0) and h4_2:pivot (via h2_0) are reached. h5_2:obtain (AND of h4_2, h4_0 and h3_0) is then reached, so crown:obtain (OR) is reached. The blocks only cut two other paths: h3_1:traverse and h5_0:escalate depend solely on h1_0, and h5_1 is blocked directly.\"}"
